bug: live state is published first and filled in afterwards, one EDT round trip per builder call (addTo, .mouse, .modelFps), so ticks and clicks see half built widgets and handler sets; converge to the build detached then install in one EDT block of onKey and newContent. applied; the reverse (.mouse/.onKey/.modelFps add to the existing handlers instead of replacing them, so .style composes and saved builders stay live) refused, it removes the only way to drop handlers; extended to whole model tasks (a sequence of mutations in one handler, like clear then add, is laid out, rendered and rehovered only when the task ends) applied; extended to whole events (all handlers of one click, mouse event, hover transition or model tick run as one task, like key dispatch) applied. proposed 4
bug: size at a given width is only asked one level down and only of direct flow children (MutableBorderLayout.wrapped); nested Panes and Borders in Border slots are measured unwrapped, so their content is clipped instead of wrapping; one Sk.sizeFor used by every layout for every child. applied. proposed 1
bug: style and drawing values (insets, sizes, radius, text height, painter coordinates) are bounded by the primary screen size, so the same program is valid on one machine and crashes on another (and a painter filling a panel wider than the screen aborts the app); use one fixed machine independent limit, keep the screen only for window placement. applied. proposed 1
bug: Frame rules applied only once at start (root pane style forced by forceTopStyle, maximized conflicts with location and size), so the same call behaves differently before and after start through a saved reference; enforce each rule where it cannot be skipped (render time, or at the offending call). applied. proposed 1
bug: window geometry checks after start (setResizable with a size, location) compare against the current window position or size, which the user controls by dragging and resizing, so the same program and clicks either work or crash; check only against program owned values and the screen, before any state changes. applied; the reverse direction (check against the live user dragged geometry) refused (it noted that a centred window growing via .fixedSize is never location checked, and that .maximized stays set after the user drags the window, and that a live .decorated adds a title bar with no fit check). proposed 12
bug: .onKey swaps in a new key manager with an empty held set, so a key held across the swap never delivers .released to the map whose .pressed fired; flush the old manager held keys before removing it. applied. proposed 1
consistency: Frame (location, resizable, fixedSize) and Graphics (position, line, rect, oval) take only typed values (XInt, WidthNat...) under the plain name, while Widget setters offer a plain Nat form plus a primed typed form; converge to the Widget way. applied. proposed 1
bug: hover (button rollover, Entered/Exited) is recomputed only on mouse motion, while press/click hit testing is live; a relayout, clear, content swap or program driven window move under a still pointer leaves stale hover until the pointer moves; re-hover from the live pointer after geometry changes. applied. proposed 1
bug: Widget settings accepted and silently ignored by some widgets (foreground on Pane/Border never reaches the painter; heightGap/widthGap on Button/Label do nothing); a widget offers a setting only if it honours it: gaps, mouse and paint on a shared container type, container foreground as the painter starting colour. applied. proposed 1
performance: every repaint tick recomputes, per widget, values that depend only on style fields changed in EDT setters (text shaping key string, font metrics, painter setup when no painter is set, boringGray clear colour, colour conversions); compute once in the setter or skip defaults, so a still GUI allocates nothing per frame. applied. proposed 1
bug: a key is identified only by an unchecked name string: KeyStroke# accepts any string ("Space", "a", "ESC") that then silently never matches; check KeyStroke names against the fixed Java key name set with a clear error, and pair held keys per physical key (code and location) so left and right Shift are distinct. applied. proposed 1
bug: explicit window sizes (fixedSize/resizable with a size, and the decoration swap) set the outer frame including title bar and borders, so the content area the program draws in and measures (panelWidth, widget sizes, mouse coordinates) differs per OS, theme and decoration; sizes given by the program are content sizes. applied. proposed 1
simplification: the runtime stores style and geometry values boxed as Fearless objects (insets, radius, text size, gaps, fps, locations) and unboxes them in every layout and paint, while setters already compute and discard the checked number; store Java numbers once in the setter, rebuild the Fearless value in the getter; drop the dead frameH and duplicated frameW state. applied. proposed 1
bug: boundary values inside ranges: Rect.contains is inclusive at right/bottom (x+width), so a width 10 rect claims 11 columns, adjacent tiles share edges, and it disagrees with drawing and widget hit testing; Hue# accepts 1.0, a second spelling of 0.0 (unequal, normalize changes it). reported: the inclusive contains is pinned by RectTests and GridHitTestTests and the tic tac toe fix clamped around it, so changing it is a decision for the user. proposed 1
